  "title": "The #1 Reason Your LOIs Keep Getting Rejected",
  "date": "2025-06-03T14:31:40.811Z",
  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n It\u2019s not the price. It\u2019s that you\u2019re ignoring the seller\u2019s ask.\n\n The #1 Reason Your LOIs Keep Getting Rejected \nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s talk about the last \u201cA\u201d in my M.A.F.I.A. framework: Asking Price.\nNo, this isn\u2019t just the number on the listing. This is about understanding what the seller actually wants\u2014and if you skip this step, your offer might go straight in the trash.\nI see this mistake constantly. A buyer does all the right things\u2014market research, adjusted EBITDA, checks financing, studies industry multiples\u2014and then they drop a number without ever asking...\n\u201cWhat does the seller actually care about?\u201d\nHere are some things to consider:\nIs the seller trying to lease you the building they own?\nDo they want to make sure their team stays employed?\nAre they emotionally attached to their client base?\nThese things matter a lot. And if your LOI doesn\u2019t speak to them, you\u2019ll lose to someone whose offer is lower but smarter.\nHere\u2019s how to fix it:\nUse the seller\u2019s language in your LOI.\n\nReference things they mentioned in emails or calls.\n\nShow them you listened\u2014and that your offer reflects their goals, not just your spreadsheet.\n\nIt\u2019s not about caving to every demand. It\u2019s about being strategic with your positioning and human in your approach. Sellers want to feel like their legacy isn\u2019t going to be bulldozed.\nSo next time you draft that LOI, think less like a banker and more like a partner. \nAddress their \u201cask\u201d in every sense of the word.\nNeed help writing a letter of intent that actually gets accepted? Deal Academy has a whole course on it.\nTo LOIs that get a second look,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
